# Options common to every supported JVM.
#
# Cassandra 4.0 and later split the JVM configuration per major Java version:
# garbage collector and GC logging flags belong in jvm11-server.options and
# jvm17-server.options, which the package ships and which this file must not
# duplicate. Keeping CMS or -XX:+PrintGCDetails here, as earlier revisions of
# this file did, prevents the JVM from starting at all on Java 17, since both
# were removed after Java 8.

-ea

-XX:+UseThreadPriorities

-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError

-Xss256k

-XX:+AlwaysPreTouch

-XX:+UseTLAB
-XX:+ResizeTLAB
-XX:+UseNUMA

-XX:+PerfDisableSharedMem

-Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true
